# Complements artio.fixv with literal FIX strings from other Artio tests (Java octal escapes
# evaluated): BusinessRejectRefIdExtractorTest, PossDupFinderTest, PasswordCleanerTest,
# FixMessagePredicateTest, SessionParserTest and further ReceiverEndPointTest framing cases.
# Many of these fixtures carry stale BodyLength/CheckSum values because the code under test
# does not check them; the vectors record what glaze's validate must say (recomputed with python3).
# Not ported: ReplayerTest (SendingTime is a runtime constant), PossDupFinderTest validate of
# SECOND_MESSAGE (only correct if BodyLength "0065" with leading zeros is accepted), PasswordCleaner
# outputs with "***" (same stale-trailer pattern), MessageBasedAcceptorSystemTest (built at runtime).

id = artio.ioi_parse
source = real-logic/artio:artio-core/src/test/java/uk/co/real_logic/artio/BusinessRejectRefIdExtractorTest.java::shouldExtractBusinessRejectRefId
kind = parse
msg = 8=FIX.4.4|9=154|35=6|49=FOO|56=BAR|34=2|52=20200505-09:48:58|23=224553|28=N|55=BAZ|54=1|27=3000|44=22333.000000|25=H|10=170|
expect = ok
count = 15
note = IOI (35=6) message; tag=value scan succeeds (15 fields)

id = artio.ioi_validate
source = real-logic/artio:artio-core/src/test/java/uk/co/real_logic/artio/BusinessRejectRefIdExtractorTest.java::shouldExtractBusinessRejectRefId
kind = validate
msg = 8=FIX.4.4|9=154|35=6|49=FOO|56=BAR|34=2|52=20200505-09:48:58|23=224553|28=N|55=BAZ|54=1|27=3000|44=22333.000000|25=H|10=170|
expect = error
note = stated BodyLength 154 but actual body is 101 bytes (CheckSum 170 also wrong, actual 123); extractor does not validate

